{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "What a client owes the server when the connection comes back. A gap is not just a pause: beliefs formed before it may be stale (a peer who stopped typing while the socket was down never sent the stop), server-side watches die with the stream that carried them (presence), and changes that happened during the gap were never delivered. Until R8 none of the five apps did any of the three: they subscribed and read when the conversation list loaded and when a chat opened, and a reconnect is neither. The one case that must NOT refresh is a session that ended — being kicked or having the token expire is terminal, the core does not reconnect by design, and re-subscribing on the way out is work for a session that no longer exists.",
  "work": {
    "dropStaleBeliefs": "Forget what could have gone stale unobserved — the typing roster above all. A belief's own ttl would clear it eventually; the gap is the moment we know it is unreliable.",
    "resubscribe": "Ask the server again for what it was watching for us. A presence subscription is a stream, and a stream dies with its connection; the client core already forgets its own bookkeeping when the stream ends, so nothing but the app is stopping a fresh subscribe.",
    "reread": "Read the current value of what is on screen. A subscription tells you about changes from now on; it says nothing about the change you missed while you were away."
  },
  "driver": "Feed the phases in order; each one answers the work it creates. An unchanged phase creates none. Phases are the kit's `FlareConnectionPhase` values.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a first connection does no extra work",
      "phases": [
        "connecting",
        "connected"
      ],
      "expect": [
        {
          "dropStaleBeliefs": false,
          "resubscribe": false,
          "reread": false
        },
        {
          "dropStaleBeliefs": false,
          "resubscribe": false,
          "reread": false
        }
      ],
      "note": "The app's own open path subscribes and reads; doing it again here would double every cold start."
    },
    {
      "name": "a connection that was never up does not count as interrupted",
      "phases": [
        "connecting",
        "connecting",
        "offline"
      ],
      "expect": [
        {
          "dropStaleBeliefs": false,
          "resubscribe": false,
          "reread": false
        },
        {
          "dropStaleBeliefs": false,
          "resubscribe": false,
          "reread": false
        },
        {
          "dropStaleBeliefs": false,
          "resubscribe": false,
          "reread": false
        }
      ]
    },
